      {
        "author": "Hattie Franken",
        "rating": 4,
        "text": "Adjusted from 1 to 4 stars as first impression matters.\n\nProperty Management hired them and just one guy showed up after Mondays storm. When he saw the tree he said he quoted too little and needed to negotiate a new estimate. Even though they initially underestimated the job, Mike was great, He never was the issue. He got hurt and took care of himself like he should. He called me the next day apologizing profusely that he was yelled at due to the initial review. Apparently the person he reported himself sick to was on leave and  manager called me later that they figured out that was the reason",
        "relativeTime": "4 years ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Nicole Welling",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "Very frustrated - paid $185 and specifically asked for weed treatment - the weeds are thriving so I essentially paid $185 to have the lawn mowed. The crew was late so I assumed maybe they forgot to spray and asked if maybe they could come back and spray when I noticed the weeds were growing back up a few days later. It’s been weeks now and they haven’t sent anyone. Asked me to set up another appointment and then never offered any times. I followed up again and even gave them a heads up that I was going to write this review and still no response. I recommend finding someone else to take care of",
        "relativeTime": "3 years ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Patty LAVIN",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "1) Was charged double fee for 1st time service for additional work. Only worked 40 minutes for $150 and never made over charge right.\n2) Was never asked about over seeding so we requested over seeding for winter lawn 2 weeks ago and was told owner would make contact. Still have not heard back.\n3) Was told irrigation would be addressed as part of initial visit. Find out only sprinklers system timer is checked as part of service. Sprinkler timer was still too much as flooding in areas continued.\n4) We have hired an outside company to investigate leak. 3 Sprinkler heads were broken and one sectio",
        "relativeTime": "5 years ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Mark Poese",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "I have a landscape voucher through my insurance carrier, and they directed my request to BJ's Landscaping.  I submitted the request on 3 June, very early in the morning.  BJ's accepted the job (per my insurance company), but they had not contacted me by 11 June, even though I called half a dozen times.  I had my insurance company cancel the service with BJ's and use a different provider who called me within 10 minutes.",
        "relativeTime": "2 years ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Thomas Sapp",
        "rating": 1,
        "text": "We have been using BJ's Landscaping for many months now and from the very beginning we had issues with the scheduling of their crew.  We had them scheduled for once a month and they would randomly show up with no announcement and sometimes they would show up twice in one month and then not again for over a month and a half.  We worked out our contract with them to be once a month on the first Friday which worked fine for a while but now that they are owned by Trim they are back to showing up multiple times a month and charging us for it.  Their support team does not answer the phone at all and",
        "relativeTime": "3 years ago"
      },
      {
        "author": "Taylor Langdon",
        "rating": 5,
        "text": "I had my front yard done because my HOA had send me a complaint. And let me just say, they won't be complaining anymore! BJ's Landscaping did a wonderful job on my little front yard and cleaned it up to precision. From all my weeds gone, to my shrubs being cleaned up, and down to my rocks not having dead leaves around them. Ben and his team at BJ's landscaping did a great job and I will definitely continue to use them for my lawn care needs.",
        "relativeTime": "5 years ago"
      }
